# Walkthrough - Full Website Redesign (DevAuth)

I have completed a total overhaul of the application, transforming it from the previous Apple-inspired aesthetic into a modern, vibrant developer-centric platform called **DevAuth**.

## Core Renovations

### 1. New Visual Identity
- **Palette**: Shifted to a high-contrast theme using deep blues (`#0a0b1e`), vibrant purples, and emerald greens.
- **Typography**: Optimized Inter for a more brutalist, technical feel.
- **Global Styles**: Updated [globals.css](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/src/app/globals.css) with radial gradients and glassmorphism effects tailored for the new palette.

### 2. Initial Loading Experience
- **InitialLoader**: Implemented a "Gatekeeper" component in the root layout that catches the first visit.
- **LoadingScreen**: A dedicated splash screen with a sleek spinner and "Cargando Sistema" message that clears after the initial bootstrap.

### 3. Split-Screen Authentication Flow
- **AuthContainer**: A new intelligent layout that divides the screen:
  - **Social/Dev Side**: Features the [DevTips](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/src/components/auth/DevTips.tsx#25-81) component with rotating advice for developers.
  - **Form Side**: Houses the [AuthCard](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/src/components/auth/AuthCard.tsx#12-170).
- **Side-Swapping Animation**: When switching between "Log in" and "Sign up", the container gracefully swaps the positions of the tips and the form.
- **Flip-Card Integration**: Your custom flip-card design is now the centerpiece of the authentication flow, fully wired into the backend APIs.

### 4. Code Cleanup
- Removed all legacy Apple-styled components (`AppleLogo`, `GlassCard`, `PremiumButton`, `FloatingInput`).
- Resolved all import dependencies to ensure a clean, modern codebase.

## Technical Verification

